// Title: Shell Execution via Flock - Linux
// Sigma ID: 4b09c71e-4269-4111-9cdd-107d8867f0cc
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Li Ling, Andy Parkidomo, Robert Rakowski, Blake Hartstein (Bloomberg L.P.)
// Date: 2024-09-02 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1083
// Description: Detects the use of the "flock" command to execute a shell. Such behavior may be associated with
//   privilege escalation, unauthorized command execution, or to break out from restricted
//   environments.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/flock/#shell
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/linux-restricted-shell-breakout-via-linux-binary-s.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_flock_shell_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/flock" and ProcessCommandLine contains " -u ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/dash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/fish" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/zsh")
